<title>USA: Standard &amp; Poor's to put GTECH on index.</title>
<headline>Standard &amp; Poor's to put GTECH on index.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-09-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Standard &amp; Poor's said Wednesday it would replace Applied Bioscience International Inc with GTECH Holdings Corp on its S&amp;P MidCap 400 Index.</p>
<p>It said its Equities Services Group would take Applied Bioscience off the index at the close of trading September 25.</p>
<p>The group would then add GTECH to the MidCap 400 Leisure time (Products) industry group, it added.</p>
<p>Standard &amp; Poor's said Applied Bioscience was merging with Pharmaceutical Product Development Inc, which was not a component of any of its indices.</p>
<p>Pharmaceutical would not be added to the index, either, it added.</p>
<p>Based in West Greenwich, Rhode Island, GTECH operates and supplies computerized on-line lottery systems.</p>
</text>
